SUMMARY:Advent Masterworks for Trumpet and Organ
DESCRIPTION:First Reformed Church of Lancaster will host a free 30-minute concert\, “Advent Masterworks for Trumpet and Organ”. The performance features acclaimed local musicians Larry Hershey on organ and Doug Albert on trumpet. The carefully curated program spans seasonal masterworks and festive arrangements: J.S. Bach: A brilliant transcription of the fourth movement of Bach’s masterly cantata\, “Wachet auf\, ruft uns die Stimme” Hans-André Stamm: A spirited\, uplifting march on the Advent carol “Wachet auf\, ruft uns die Stimme” Christina Harmon: A beautifully textured arrangement of “O Come\, O Come\, Emmanuel” Marc Cheban: A grand\, solo organ performance of “Grand Fantasia on Joy to the World\,” performed by Mr. Hershey Maurice André: A brilliant finale featuring Mr. Albert on the piccolo trumpet on “Gloria in excelsis Deo.” \n\n\n\nEvent Details: Date: Friday\, December 4 Time: 8:00 PM (30-minute duration) Location: First Reformed Church\, 40 E. Orange St.\, Lancaster\, PA AdmissionFree and open to the public; a freewill offering will be received. Come enjoy a beautiful\, reflective half-hour of world-class sacred music to usher in the Advent season. \n\n\n\n\n    Learn More
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/advent-masterworks-for-trumpet-and-organ/
LOCATION:First Reformed Church\, 40 East Orange Street\, Lancaster\, Pennsylvania\, 17602\, United States
CATEGORIES:Arts & Entertainment
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2026/11/larry-and-doug.avif
ORGANIZER;CN="First Reformed Church":MAILTO:webmaster.FRCLancaster@gmail.com
END:VEVENT
